{"id": "EUVD-2026-108919", "enisaUuid": "f68e4ca8-9012-3e24-a4d4-b7de5b18300d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: steam: Rearrange teardown sequence\n\nThis fixes a narrow window during the teardown sequence where callbacks\ncould still be scheduled during cleanup that would then have a dangling\npointer to the now-freed steam struct.\n\nThis also puts work canceling for rumble and mode switch in\nsteam_unregister, as that shouldn't persist while the client hdev is open.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2587923d50c8b141ce0ccb284c714cf6054d6a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81a8209c09f9be7eef860ca6cc154749a6b4d243", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86724f4bcf6049c3a322f7a7b1f968210059c46a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5ea938ff776306798d3a11485c2475034f92131", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ddce9641ce924ed91ec8304577e463823a29ffaf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98945"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2726f149-61b7-3fc1-8da1-7331b35cc130", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2ea34c0a-9faa-3c8a-a765-573f6cbce3eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <d2587923d50c8b141ce0ccb284c714cf6054d6a7"}, {"id": "700371af-c627-36f4-800d-e5dc2a56173c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.18.57"}, {"id": "8676e2fd-0e95-3d3d-af57-e7d6bfa4fdb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <ddce9641ce924ed91ec8304577e463823a29ffaf"}, {"id": "a7227549-0fef-3df8-aa0e-b3675247b9a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "a94ddaed-6deb-32fb-b0b2-feba6715e